  "id": "U31",
  "kind": "usage",
  "description": "The attribute set changes mid-session (experiments.ids arrives after the first export, as Gemini loads experiments asynchronously): the old series keep being exported unchanged and new series with the same start appear. The new series count from 0 (sibling rule G5, same session, model and start), so their tokens are neither lost nor double counted; the unchanged old series contribute 0.",
  "contract": "ADR-0016 Changes 2026-10-29 (S5b QA findings G5/G15) New sibling series (\"A series that first appears for a (session, model, start) whose sibling series already have baselines counts from 0\"); Changes 2026-10-29 (S5b review V1) R4 (series = all point attributes + startNs; deltas summed), R2 (\"This makes the G5 sibling rule a special case\"), R5, R6; telemetryAttributes.ts (experiments.ids only when experiments are loaded); Vertex AI pricing page (fetched 2026-10-29)",
  "ambiguities": ["G2", "G3", "G21"],
